  "body": "Deadline sale: Closes on Thursday 19 November 2026 at 2:00PM  (unless sold prior)\r\n\r\nWalk up to blue sky and palm trees, and the sense of calm begins. Tucked away as the end home in the collection, this is a private retreat with the largest landscaped backyard, a corner balcony wrapped in trees and birdsong, and sea views drifting out to the Hauraki Gulf, all just moments from Torbay Village and the beach.\r\n\r\nSpanning approx. 180m² of gross building area on a generous 215m² freehold site, this home offers four bedrooms, three bathrooms and extra outdoor living space. A double garage plus additional off-street parking with plenty of room for your boat or camper make family life even easier, while a 10-Year Master Build Guarantee provides lasting peace of mind.\r\n\r\nEnjoy the sea views, from sweeping panoramas across the Hauraki Gulf to a peaceful outlook over treetops to the water. Upstairs, high stud ceilings and designer skylights enhance a spacious, multifunctional living area and an extra-large kitchen with an island bench. The space opens onto the corner balcony, the perfect spot for your first coffee of the day among the treetops. Two bedrooms are also on this level, including the master bedroom with its own sea view, a well-appointed ensuite and a generous walk-in wardrobe.\r\n\r\nDownstairs is all about flexibility, with two spacious bedrooms and a laundry to make family living easy. Set at the rear of the collection, this home enjoys a larger garden and greater privacy, with a private deck for relaxing or entertaining.\r\n\r\nLocal shops and cafés are just moments away, with Waiake Beach, Long Bay Regional Park and boat and kayak launching close by. The home is zoned for Torbay School, Northcross Intermediate and Long Bay College.\r\n\r\nA private end home with a garden this generous rarely comes along so close to the sand. The seller has given clear instructions to sell. Enquire today and secure your new home for summer!",
